cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Salt Season Tracker or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Salt Season Tracker: a live map of road-salt pulses in U.S. streams"
abstract: >-
  The Salt Season Tracker downloads daily mean specific conductance (and
  streamflow, where measured) from U.S. Geological Survey stream sensors in the
  lower 48 states every morning and compares each stream with its own May-October
  level. It maps winter road-salt pulses, detects regional salt storms, scores
  every stream and state over the season (peak, days at 3x and above, recovery
  after a pulse, between-storm level), archives past winters back to 2016-17, and
  describes each station's upstream watershed (EPA StreamCat metrics, land-use
  classes after Chen and Husic, 2026). Code, daily data files and winter archives
  are open.
